<title>PORTUGAL: Portuguese bond report.</title>
<headline>Portuguese bond report.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bonds were being lifted by the strengthening Spanish market even if the mood remains cautious, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;There is still a lot of dust in the air,&quot; said one trader refering to the recent market sell-off that had been triggered by concerns that southern European countries would not win entry to the single currency.</p>
<p>After a cautious start, the market was taking its lead from Spain where bond prices rose after the Treasury left the market short of three and 10-year paper at its auction.</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
